wlcore: the NVS file is optional, request it without a warning

wl18xx runs without an NVS file (the MAC address comes from the chip's
fuse and wlcore_nvs_cb already handles a missing file at debug level),
and the firmware loader's "Direct firmware load for
ti-connectivity/wl1271-nvs.bin failed with error -2" at ERR level is the
only trace of a rootfs that ships none. Ask for it the way the loader
provides for optional files.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Scott Wiederhold <s.e.wiederhold@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wlcore/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wlcore/main.c
@@ -6799,8 +6799,8 @@
 	if (pdev_data->family && pdev_data->family->nvs_name) {
 		nvs_name = pdev_data->family->nvs_name;
-		ret = request_firmware_nowait(THIS_MODULE, FW_ACTION_UEVENT,
-					      nvs_name, &pdev->dev, GFP_KERNEL,
-					      wl, wlcore_nvs_cb);
+		ret = firmware_request_nowait_nowarn(THIS_MODULE, nvs_name,
+						     &pdev->dev, GFP_KERNEL,
+						     wl, wlcore_nvs_cb);
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			wl1271_error("request_firmware_nowait failed for %s: %d",
 				     nvs_name, ret);
